---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import data from '../data/benchmarks.json';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const { ci, builds, targets } = data;
const kernels = ci.kernels;
const met = kernels.filter((kernel) => kernel.percent >= targets.jit).length;
// The bars run past 100%, since release builds aim beyond the target.
const scale = 125;
const at = (percent: number) => `${(percent / scale) * 100}%`;
---

<Base title="Benchmarks" description="Fennec's real benchmark numbers against its speed targets, measured in CI. In progress.">
  <section class="wrap head">
    <span class="pill">In progress</span>
    <h1>Benchmarks</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Every kernel has a speed target, and these are real numbers from CI against it. They aren't where we want them yet.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Speed against target</h2>
    <p class="note">
      Each target comes from idiomatic code for the same work in the fastest established systems language, built with overflow checks, as Fennec is. Each engine aims for its own share of the target, marked on every bar: the interpreter's {targets.interpreter[0]}–{targets.interpreter[1]}% as a band, the JIT's {targets.jit}%, going to {targets.jit_later}% later, and {targets.release}% for release builds, which don't exist yet. These numbers are the JIT's.
    </p>
    <div class="table">
      <div class="tr th">
        <span>Kernel</span><span class="num">Startup</span><span class="num">Work</span><span>Work's speed, % of target</span>
      </div>
      {
        kernels.map((kernel) => (
          <div class="tr">
            <span class="name">{kernel.name}</span>
            <span class="num">{kernel.startup_ms.toFixed(1)} ms</span>
            <span class="num">{kernel.work_ms.toFixed(1)} ms</span>
            <span class="bar-cell">
              <span class="track">
                <span class="band" style={`left: ${at(targets.interpreter[0])}; width: ${at(targets.interpreter[1] - targets.interpreter[0])}`} title={`Interpreter target: ${targets.interpreter[0]}–${targets.interpreter[1]}%`} />
                <span class="fill" style={`width: ${at(Math.min(kernel.percent, scale))}`} />
                <span class="mark" style={`left: ${at(targets.jit)}`} title={`JIT target: ${targets.jit}%`} />
                <span class="mark" style={`left: ${at(targets.release)}`} title={`Release target: ${targets.release}%`} />
              </span>
              <strong>{kernel.percent.toFixed(0)}%</strong>
            </span>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      {met} of {kernels.length} kernels are at the JIT's target. Against a target using a slower, attack-resistant default hash instead, <code>dicts</code> reaches {ci.dicts_default_hash_percent.toFixed(0)}%, which isn't counted here. From commit <code>{ci.commit}</code> on {ci.date}, on {ci.machine}. Speed is counted in instructions, which barely move when a machine is busy, so it can differ from the times shown. Times are medians of repeated runs, and they move by several percent between runs. Once a kernel reaches the JIT's target, CI fails if it drops below.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>Build and test times</h2>
    <p class="note">Measured on {builds.machine}, at commit <code>{builds.commit}</code>, on {builds.kit}.</p>
    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat"><strong>{builds.one_function_s} s</strong><span>to rebuild after changing one function</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><strong>{builds.first_s.toFixed(0)} s</strong><span>for its first build, with an empty cache. We want this much lower.</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><strong>&lt;{builds.tests_unchanged_s} s</strong><span>to rerun tests when nothing they depend on changed, on one small test file</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <h2>How it's measured</h2>
    <p>
      Each target is pinned once per architecture, from reference code built at full optimization, with overflow checks, for that architecture's baseline CPU, and each kernel must print what its reference prints. Startup is everything before <code>main</code>; only the work counts toward the target. A failure is fixed in the compiler, never by changing the benchmark. The kernels and the
      method are in <a href="https://github.com/fennec-language/fennec/tree/main/bench">the repository</a>, and you can{' '}
      <a href={`${base}speed/`}>read how the two speeds are designed</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  section {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
  }

  .head {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }

  .pill {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.75rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 7vw, 3.6rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .note {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .table {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
  }

  .tr {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.8fr 0.9fr 2.2fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.7rem 1.1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .tr:first-child {
    border-top: 0;
  }

  .th {
    background: var(--surface);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .name {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .num {
    text-align: right;
  }

  .bar-cell {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .bar-cell strong {
    width: 2.75rem;
    text-align: right;
  }

  .band {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 auto 0 0;
    background: var(--border);
  }

  .mark {
    position: absolute;
    top: -3px;
    bottom: -3px;
    width: 2px;
    background: var(--text, currentColor);
  }

  .track {
    position: relative;
    flex: 1;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--surface-strong);
  }

  .fill {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 auto 0 0;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent-bright);
  }

  .stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .stat {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--surface);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem;
  }

  .stat strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 2rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .stat span {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .tr {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 0.35rem 1rem;
    }

    .th {
      display: none;
    }

    .tr .num {
      text-align: left;
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--muted);
    }

    .name,
    .bar-cell {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }
</style>
